    "collapsible-content": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "faq-lasts": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long will the 90-Day Reset last?",
            "row_content": "<p>About 90 days of daily use for one person. Lotion is what you use most — morning, after showers, after handwashing — so you get three full-size bottles. The cream stretches much further because a little goes a long way, so one jar covers the whole window. If you're applying to a large area twice a day, it may run a little shorter; on the face and hands only, it often lasts longer.<\/p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq-subscription": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is this a subscription?",
            "row_content": "<p>No. The 90-Day Reset is a one-time order — no auto-billing, no commitment. When you're ready to restock, you can reorder or start a subscribe-and-save plan then, but nothing recurring is set up by buying this box.<\/p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq-results": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long until I see results?",
            "row_content": "<p>Most customers feel the difference at first application — the lotion absorbs within minutes, the cream forms a soft barrier overnight. Real changes in dry-patch frequency or chronic reactivity typically take 2–3 weeks of consistent use, and skin usually keeps improving over the full 90 days. That's exactly why we sized this as a 90-day box instead of a single bottle.<\/p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq-eczema": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Will this work if I have eczema, rosacea, or sensitive skin?",
            "row_content": "<p>We can't make medical claims and don't sell our products as treatments. What we can tell you: we built these formulas around what reactive skin most often doesn't tolerate — synthetic fragrance, parabens, mineral oil, dimethicone, lanolin. Many of our customers with eczema, rosacea, or perioral dermatitis report fewer reactions on this routine than on conventional drugstore lotions. If you've reacted to multiple products before, the Pure Unscented option is the closest thing we offer to a clean-slate routine.<\/p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq-patch-test": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Should I patch test first?",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes — especially if you've reacted to multiple products in the past. Apply a small amount to the inside of your wrist or behind your ear and wait 24 hours. No redness, itching, or stinging means you're clear to use it elsewhere. The lotion absorbs faster, so it's the easier of the two to patch test first.<\/p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq-react": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What if my skin reacts to the reset?",
            "row_content": "<p>Email us within 30 days. We'll refund you and you don't need to send anything back. We mean it — sensitive skin shouldn't have to gamble on a product that didn't work, and we'd rather know what triggered the reaction so we can keep refining what we make.<\/p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq-scent": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Which scent should I choose?",
            "row_content": "<p>Choose <strong>Pure Unscented<\/strong> if you have reactive skin or simply don't want any fragrance — it's our most sensitive-skin-friendly option, with no essential oils added. The lightly scented options use natural aromatics if you prefer a subtle coconut or botanical note. All scents share the same clean base formula.<\/p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq-when": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Lotion vs. cream — when do I use each?",
            "row_content": "<p>Lotion in the morning and after showers — it absorbs in minutes and won't leave a residue under clothes. Cream at night, on dry patches, hands, feet, elbows, knees — anywhere skin needs more than a daytime lotion can give. The two work as a system: lotion for daily moisture, cream for repair.<\/p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "faq-lasts",
        "faq-subscription",
        "faq-results",
        "faq-eczema",
        "faq-patch-test",
        "faq-react",
        "faq-scent",
        "faq-when"
      ],
